From c694fb4800814bb7f6b465dc635dcbbff528b7b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:11:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 274/274] usb: typec: tcpm: Don't answer unexpected VDM
 responses with Not_Supported

A Structured VDM that matches no alternate mode, arrives outside a VDM
AMS, and finds no Discover Identity response configured (nr_snk_vdo == 0)
is answered with Not_Supported on PD 3.x. That is right for a request
the port does not support, but the same path is taken by a response
(ACK, NAK or BUSY) that does not belong to an outstanding request, most
often one that arrives after VDMResponseTimer expired. A response is
not a request and must not be answered; worse, the port partner may take
the Not_Supported as the reply to whatever it sends next, or, as seen
with a USB-C DP/USB3 dongle, answer it with a Not_Supported of its own:

  AMS DISCOVER_SVIDS finished     <- VDMResponseTimer expired
  PD RX, header: 0x248f [1]       <- the late Discover SVIDs ACK
  PD TX, header: 0xbb0            <- Not_Supported from tcpm
  ...
  PD RX, header: 0x690 [1]        <- Not_Supported from the dongle

Drop unexpected Structured VDM responses instead, and log them.

Fixes: a20dcf53ea98 ("usb: typec: tcpm: Respond Not_Supported if no snk_vdo")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
index 3253355b1..0445db4ef 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -2827,6 +2827,16 @@ static void tcpm_handle_vdm_request(struct tcpm_port *port,
 		port->vdm_sm_running = true;
 		rlen = tcpm_pd_svdm(port, adev, p, cnt, response, &adev_action,
 				    rx_sop_type, &response_tx_sop_type);
+	} else if (PD_VDO_SVDM(p[0]) && PD_VDO_CMDT(p[0]) != CMDT_INIT) {
+		/*
+		 * A Structured VDM response (ACK, NAK or BUSY) that does not
+		 * belong to an outstanding request, for example one that
+		 * arrives after VDMResponseTimer expired. Not_Supported is the
+		 * reply to a request the port does not support, and must not be
+		 * sent for a response: the port partner may take it as a reply
+		 * to its next message. Drop it.
+		 */
+		tcpm_log(port, "Ignoring unexpected VDM response 0x%08x", p[0]);
 	} else {
 		if (port->negotiated_rev >= PD_REV30)
 			tcpm_pd_handle_msg(port, PD_MSG_CTRL_NOT_SUPP, NONE_AMS);
-- 
2.55.0

